        "text": "According to Nevada Department of Human Resources (Petitioners), according to Nevada Department of Human Resources (Petitioners), petitioners argue that Congress did not validly abrogate state sovereign immunity when it enacted the Family Medical Leave Act\u2019s family\u2011leave provision, because the FMLA is ordinary economic legislation, not antidiscrimination legislation, there was no discernible pattern of unconstitutional state behavior, and the 12\u2011week mandate is not a proportional response."
      },
