            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Nevada Department of Human Resources (Petitioners), according to Nevada Department of Human Resources (Petitioners), petitioners also contend that Congress was concerned the FMLA might be challenged under the Equal Protection Clause and therefore framed the law as promoting equal employment opportunity."
